    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0387" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg337"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Smythe.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic">January 31,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A copy of your No. 23, of the 10th instant,
                    in regard to the case of the American schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Water
                        Witch</hi>, which arrived in Haytian waters with 2 cannon and 60 pounds of
                    powder on board, having been transmitted to the Secretary of the Treasury, that
                    official has replied to your inquiry whether sailing vessels of the United
                    States are allowed to carry an armament as ship’s stores, or otherwise, that the
                    laws do not forbid the carrying of articles of the character mentioned, provided
                    there shall be no violation of Chapter LXVII of the Revised Statutes.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
